    "result_text": "The test passes. Let me summarize the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented \"open a client \u2192 see the projects I'm doing for them\" as a small, additive full-stack change.\n\n**Backend** (projects feature \u2014 clients does not import it):\n- `ProjectRepository.java` \u2014 added `findByClient(long clientId)` (extracted a shared `RowMapper`), a `WHERE p.client_id = ?` variant of the existing joined query.\n- `ProjectsGetLogic.java` \u2014 `GET /api/projects` now takes an optional `?clientId=<id>` query param (same idiom as `/api/invoices?projectId=`); blank/absent still returns all projects, so existing behavior is unchanged.\n\n**Frontend** (clients feature):\n- New `features/clients/ClientProjects.tsx` \u2014 owns its own state, fetches `/api/projects?clientId=<id>`, and renders `client-projects-table` reusing the `project-row-<id>` / `project-name` anchors the spec expects.\n- `ClientsPage.tsx` \u2014 each client row gets a `client-open-<id>` button; opening one renders `ClientProjects` for that client.\n\n**No DB migration** was needed \u2014 `projects.client_id` already exists (V3), so the request required no schema change; adding an empty migration would be non-additive noise.\n\n`bin/e2e` passes (1/1). No pinned scaffolding or the test spec was touched.",
